React to Next.js Converter (react-to-next-converter)

A lightweight, experimental VS Code extension built to automate common migration tasks when converting standard React components into Next.js App Router compatible files using Abstract Syntax Tree (AST) parsing with @babel/parser.

🚀 About This Project

This project was built purely as a personal hobby and experimental project at home, created with AI guidance and collaboration (Gemini). It was developed as a creative exploration into AST code manipulation, VS Code extension development, and React/Next.js migration patterns.

✨ Features

Client Directive Injection: Automatically adds 'use client' to components containing interactive React hooks (useState, useEffect, etc.) or event handlers.

Image Optimization: Converts standard HTML <img> elements to Next.js <Image /> components (next/image).

Link Transformation: Updates standard <a> tags and React Router <Link> components to Next.js <Link> (next/link).

Router Hook Migration: Converts react-router-dom navigation hooks (like useNavigate) to Next.js App Router equivalents (useRouter from next/navigation).

💡 Usage for Developers

Other developers are welcome to study, fork, use, or build upon this codebase to create their own tools or custom migration scripts.

If you find this repository helpful for learning about AST transformations or VS Code extensions, feel free to use it as a base for your own creative projects!

